This directory must exist before the storage service writes its first image, and
nothing creates it at runtime.

CachedImageStorage.__init__ (cltl-backend/src/cltl/backend/impl/cached_storage.py)
does `os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(self._storage_path))`, which creates the
PARENT of `./storage/image` and not `./storage/image` itself. It is a known bug —
cltl-dev/integration/tests/slices/test_backend_storage.py calls it out — and the
way it fails is the worst kind: `cv2.imwrite` into a missing directory returns
False rather than raising, so the PUT that stores an uploaded image answers
`204 No Content` and the GET that fetches it later answers `KeyError: No image
with id ...`. Nothing anywhere says "the directory does not exist".

So the directory is committed. Do not delete it. See docs/gotchas.md.
